('Every inert saved continuation payload is automatically executed later even when no initiating channel is configured.','If true, storing the bytes would guarantee a later executing actor without a configured initiator.','The session ends with an inert JSON file, no watcher/scheduler and no later user resumption; the file persists but no executing actor exists.','Payload persistence and an initiating event are distinct causal requirements.','The current capsule can be classified saved-only while the current active run continues independently.','A genuinely configured scheduler would supply the missing external initiator, not make the inert payload self-initiate. BEDROCK-LOGIC: inert data does not execute absent an actor/channel.','REJECTED','The no-initiator state defeats every; the scheduler boundary is compatible with the corrected account.'),
